## Session 8 summary

**Major progress: 8/tcp suite went 12/17 → 15/17 (twice, runs 109/110), with the historical #1 and #2 blockers (dlm_fairness, dir_reuse in-suite) both now PASSING.** Current build `38D787B1`, deployed and verified.

**Fixes landed and RULE-4-proven this session:**
1. **FIX-21** — selective AG-grant migration at `xfs_trans_dup`: only AGs still referenced by pending defer work items keep their DLM grants across rolls (preserves the sess26 EFI guard exactly). Killed the cross-AG hold-and-wait convoy: `P1-AGWAIT` held-sets went empty, dlm_fairness 3/8 → 7/8.
2. **FIX-22** — the SF rebase-union (`mxfs_dir_rebase_shortform`) re-grafted our own un-destaged removes from stale disk images (traced name-by-name via new P8-SFRM/SFIFLUSH/SFADOPT ledgers: `mv n7_r49 → .done`, union re-imported `n7_r49` 5ms later). Filter the disk image through the per-tenure removed-set → dlm_fairness **PASS 8/8, first ever** (run103), zero leftovers.
3. **FIX-24** — demote-wait rescue poll 30s→3s: run106 proved each dir_reuse "stall" was ONE node sleeping the full 30s on a zombie DEMOTING inode before the (instant) rescue arms ran → dir_reuse **PASS 8/8 in-suite, first ever** (runs 109+110).
4. **FIX-25** — live-stack-proven 3-task deadlock: bast drain waits on folio writeback ← folio needs `xfs_end_ioend`'s unwritten conversion ← needs ILOCK EX ← blocked by that same drain. Added `xfs_task_in_ioend()` admit arms (nested EX while mirror still EX).
5. **FIX-23 attempted and REVERTED** (run107 regression: gen-0 release on acquire timeout kills live grants in the re-affirm case — documented in code).
6. **Harness**: cascade guards in run.sh (pkill + `fuser -k -m` on test timeout — leftover processes were poisoning 3-5 downstream tests per run); soak's dmesg-clean criterion was failing on our own ungated diagnostic `dump_stack`s (now instr-gated).

**Root evidence secured for the next blocker** (4/tcp dir_reuse readdir undercount, reproducer ~4min): a durable intra-block tear — unused-entry chain swallows a live dirent (lookup OK, readdir misses, all nodes) — with **test2's xfsaild writing the shared dir block mid-peer-tenure (`P3W-DIRWR … skip=0`)** plus a `P-DBLALLOC` on the same daddr. The exact thread to pull (P3W skip-guard at `pal/linux/xfs_buf.c:3290`, sess40/sess16 prior leads) is written up in ccmemory `sess8-part3-readdir-tear-xfsaild-dirblock-root`.

